---
// Trang EN: COPYRIGHT — /en/copyright/
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Copyright" description="Copyright terms of Mechanical Watch Knowledge: what you may quote, how to credit, and how third-party sources are used.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16">
    <div class="mb-3 h-1 w-12 rounded bg-brass"></div>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-4xl text-navy dark:text-dark-text sm:text-5xl">Copyright terms</h1>

    <div class="prose-content mt-8">
      <h2>Site content</h2>
      <p>
        Unless stated otherwise, the articles, diagrams and illustrations on this site are the work of
        the site's editor. You are welcome to <strong>quote short excerpts with a visible link back</strong>
        to the original page. Republishing full articles, or reusing original illustrations and
        interactive diagrams without written permission, is not allowed.
      </p>

      <h2>Citing sources</h2>
      <p>
        Every article ends with a list of sources — manufacturer pages, the Fondation de la Haute
        Horlogerie, standards bodies and edited publications. Those sources belong to their respective
        owners. This site uses them as references and credits them inline; it does not reproduce
        third-party copyrighted imagery.
      </p>

      <h2>Trademarks</h2>
      <p>
        Brand names and model names (Rolex, Omega, Seiko, Submariner, Speedmaster, Tank and others)
        are trademarks of their respective owners. They appear on this site purely for identification
        and editorial discussion — no affiliation or endorsement is implied.
      </p>

      <h2>Corrections</h2>
      <p>
        If you believe content here infringes your rights, or if a source has been credited
        incorrectly, contact us via the Contact page and it will be reviewed and corrected promptly.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
